# Do the Boots of Providence pay their Luck bonus while carried, as their own
# page promises? Read by tools/check_boots_providence.sh, bead inc-izuu.
#
#   w y                      enter wizard mode and open its menu.
#   Item Acquisition         RIGHT*20 walks the glyph row to Boots: ItemGlyphs
#   RIGHT*20                 (src/Tables.cpp:341) puts -AI_BOOTS 20 steps
#                            along, and the header line names the category.
#   @until "Boots of the     the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#     Druid" DOWN            cursor is walked. Three rows show and the MIDDLE
#                            one is selected, so the run stops on the pass
#                            where the row BELOW the wanted one appears. The
#                            Druid is the entry after Providence in
#                            lib/m_items.irh. The check does not trust that
#                            ordering: it reads the boots' name back off the
#                            inventory screen.
#   3 ENTER                  the acquisition asks for the item level, which is
#                            the plus (src/Debug.cpp:619). One point of Luck
#                            per plus, so +3 is a bonus no rounding can hide.
#   t SPACE d                put the boots in the first belt slot -- CARRIED,
#                            not worn. That slot holds the starting gold,
#                            which the swap lifts into the air, and the
#                            manager will not close with anything in the air,
#                            so d drops the gold on the floor.
#   ESC d                    the character sheet, whose attribute lines print
#                            the bonus and where it came from
#                            (src/Sheet.cpp:91-99). This is the red/green
#                            reading: "(base 15)" against
#                            "(base 15, +3 magic)".
#   i t SPACE k SPACE        the same boots from the belt onto the feet. The
#                            second sheet must read the SAME +3 and not +6: a
#                            grant applied twice would show here.
#   i k SPACE d              and off the feet onto the floor. The last sheet
#                            must be back to base, because a bonus that
#                            outlives the item is worse than one that never
#                            arrives.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*20
@until "Boots of the Druid" DOWN
ENTER
3
ENTER
t
SPACE
d
@dump:boots-on-belt
ESC
d
@dump:sheet-carried
ESC
i
t
SPACE
k
SPACE
@dump:boots-worn
ESC
d
@dump:sheet-worn
ESC
i
k
SPACE
d
@dump:boots-dropped
ESC
d
@dump:sheet-dropped
